# URL routing for the site. Cloudflare applies these on deploy; web/vite.config.js
# parses this same file for `npm run dev` / `vite preview`, so the two cannot drift.
#
# ## Pretty note URLs
#
#   /note/en-US/cell-death/Eryptosis          → wiki note
#   /output/en-US/task_output_parthanatos_…   → task output
#
# Both are 200 proxies (rewrites, not redirects) to pages/md-viewer.html, which
# renders the note and points rel=canonical back at the pretty path. The browser
# URL is unchanged by a proxy, so md-viewer reads the note from
# location.pathname — the rewrite target's query never reaches the shell (see
# noteFromPathname() in md-viewer.html).
#
# WHY NOT /wiki/* AND /tasks/*: those prefixes contain the raw .md assets, and
# Cloudflare follows redirects "regardless of whether or not an asset matches
# the incoming request". A splat there therefore swallows the shell's own fetch
# of the note body, and the shell receives HTML instead of markdown (every note
# fails). There is no rule that fixes this from inside the prefix: Cloudflare
# supports only ONE trailing splat per rule, so the mid-path guard
# (`/wiki/*.md → /wiki/:splat.md`) that wrangler dev tolerates is silently
# ignored in production. Distinct prefixes are the only collision-free option.
# (Found live: `.md` fetches 307'd/200'd to the md-viewer shell.)
#
# ## Root
#
# `"html_handling": "none"` (wrangler.jsonc) disables Cloudflare's automatic
# `/` → index.html mapping, so the root rule below restores it. That setting is
# also required so `.html` URLs are not 307-stripped — which would drop the
# query string the reader iframe depends on.

/  /index.html  200
/note/*    /pages/md-viewer.html    200
/output/*  /pages/md-viewer.html    200
